Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;

register(IsCopyW);
define
    iwSrc="ORIG";
    iwBag;
    iwRun code={
        iwBag +% iwSrc;
        iwFace <- iwBag["iwSrc"];
        cerr "IW1 BEFORE any write -- the named source:":;
        addrOf(iwSrc);
        cerr "IW2 BEFORE any write -- the other face:":;
        addrOf(iwFace);
        iwSrc :. isCopY;
        cerr "IW3 AFTER  :. isCopY on the source -- source:":;
        addrOf(iwSrc);
        cerr "IW4 AFTER  :. isCopY on the source -- other face:":;
        addrOf(iwFace);
        };
    ;
iwRun();
print "PROBEISCOPYWRITE SENTINEL -- reached the foot":;
stop();

ASKS WHETHER faceT'S OPTIONS ROW IS BUILDABLE, which is a WRITE question and not
a read question. probeIsCopy already settled the read: `.isCopY` is unreadable
from incant, echoing its own tag (#26), so addrOf is the only road IN.

But faceT's row needs a road OUT as well -- it writes a bit through one face and
reads it through the other. `:.` is the setFlag operator and faceT uses it on
noPrinT. If `:. isCopY` cannot write, the row is unbuildable for a REASON THAT IS
NOT THE ONE ON RECORD: faceT omitted it because "isCopy is visible only through
addrOf, and every subject reads 1". C20 showed the column DOES discriminate -- the
subscript element reads 0 -- so the recorded reason is now half-wrong, and the
question is whether the row is nevertheless still unbuildable.

READING, and the addrOf isCopy column is the witness because the flag read is
known-dead:
  IW3 differs from IW1  ->  the write LANDED. The row is buildable and faceT
                            owes it.
  IW3 identical to IW1  ->  the write did NOT land. The row stays unbuilt, and
                            the RECORDED REASON gets corrected to the real one.
  IW4 vs IW2            ->  only meaningful if the write landed at all; it is the
                            actual crossing question and it is not asked unless
                            IW3 says there is something to ask about.
⚠ BOTH FACES ARE NAMED, so both arrive through the carrier and both are expected
to read isCopy=1 at IW1/IW2. That expectation is itself worth seeing: if the two
faces DISAGREE before any write, the column is reporting the carrier and not the
subject, and every row below is void.
